#!/bin/sh
# Post-checkout hook - rewrite the plan page from the entries this checkout now holds.
#
# `docs/wiki/plan.md` is generated where it is read and never committed (2026-11-16): committed,
# it made every open pull request conflict with every merge to main. So each checkout writes its
# own copy - after a `git worktree add`, a `git switch`, the start of a rebase - and the page
# CLAUDE.md calls the queue says what the entries say. A fresh clone runs no hook (none is armed
# yet): `make install` writes the page once, or `bun tools/backlog-plan/plan.mjs` by hand. docs/wiki/cicd.md, "The plan page is generated where it is read".
#
# The page's line is discarded (a line every switch would print is noise); a problem the generator
# finds goes to stderr. Called by git directly (`core.hooksPath` = `.husky`, tracked).
exec bun tools/backlog-plan/plan.mjs >/dev/null
